config-manager-market.disclaimer.download.text:
You are about to download configs from a public network market and import them locally.

Downloaded content is untrusted input: not officially reviewed and may carry risks (installing plugins / writing files / changing settings).
· Everything is validated and shown before import; high-risk sections are not imported by default and require individual approval;
· A snapshot is auto-created before import and rollback is available on failure;
· Please verify the source and content before confirming the import.

config-manager-market.disclaimer.upload.text:
You are about to upload configs to your public repo (<login>/dsh-configs) and submit a listing request to the official market.

Uploaded content becomes publicly visible and requires human review before entering the official market. Please ensure:
· No real secrets / credentials are included (env-var references like $VAR are safe);
· No personal privacy or local environment info is included;
· You have the right to share these configs.
